use ../../../lib/UiComponent

export ui-component TextArea:
    description:
        A text area is a box for typing several lines of text, such as a
        comment or a description. It either stays a fixed height and scrolls,
        or grows to fit what's typed.

    lines:
        Pressing Enter starts a new line. Pressing Tab moves focus out of the
        text area, as it does everywhere else, rather than typing a tab.

    height:
        The component chooses a fixed height, or a height that grows with the
        text. A growing text area can have a maximum height, after which it
        scrolls. Whether the user can drag to resize it is up to the chosen
        library.

    common:
        Its label, placeholder, help text, error message, length limit, and
        disabled and read-only states work the same way as a TextField's.

    nonGoals:
        - No formatting, such as bold or lists. That's a rich text editor
